# solidity-d: d in Solidity (#433). A modifier named in a function's header lands on its
# `modifier`, and an `emit` on its `event`. The files are written here, not in the project, which
# every other scenario counts the files of.
merl
wait Open a file (fuzzy)
run mkdir -p solshop && printf 'contract ShopToken {\n    event Minted(address to, uint256 amount);\n\n    modifier withinSupply(uint256 amount) {\n        _;\n    }\n\n    function mint(address to, uint256 amount) external withinSupply(amount) {\n        emit Minted(to, amount);\n    }\n}\n' > solshop/ShopToken.sol
key q
wait merl exited: 0
merl solshop/ShopToken.sol
wait contract ShopToken
key /
type withinSupply(amount
key Enter d
wait ShopToken.withinSupply (by name, 1 match)
merl solshop/ShopToken.sol
wait contract ShopToken
key /
type Minted(to
key Enter d
wait ShopToken.Minted (by name, 1 match)
key Escape
